      "aperture": "Aperture",
      "aperture_is_everything": "Aperture is everything",
      "aperture_is_everything_magnification_f": "Aperture is everything. Magnification = focal length / eyepiece focal length, but USEFUL magnification is capped at ~2× aperture in mm. Beyond that, you just magnify the blur. A 100 mm scope tops out around 200×; a 300 mm scope can usefully push to ~600×. The Dawes limit (resolution) and limiting magnitude (faintest visible) both scale with aperture, not magnification. \"Bigger eye, not bigger zoom.\"",
      "aperture_mm": "Aperture (mm)",
