      "a_partly_submerged_chamber_traps_a_col": "A partly submerged chamber traps a column of air above the rising and falling sea surface. As waves push the water up and down inside the chamber, the trapped air is forced in and out through a Wells turbine — which spins the same direction regardless of which way the air flows. The turbine drives a generator.",
      "a_refrigeration_cycle_that_moves_heat_": "A refrigeration cycle that moves heat between the constant-temperature ground and a home. In winter, evaporator absorbs heat from the ground loop; compressor raises temperature; condenser releases heat to the home; expansion valve resets the cycle. COP 3 to 5 means 3 to 5 units of heat moved per unit of electricity used.",
